.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Jul 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payments-create - Create a payment and sign it with the payer's key


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payments create [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a RAIL0 payment and sign the EIP-3009 payload with the payer's key in
one step (--private-key / -p). The API stores the signature; the payee can then
authorize. If --private-key is omitted, the CLI prompts for it (hidden) on a
terminal — so the key stays out of the shell history and process arguments.

.PP
--from (payer) and --to (payee) must be different addresses: a payment can't be
sent from an address to itself.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-a\fP, \fB--amount\fP=""
	Amount as a decimal in token units (e.g. '1.00' for 1 USDC); the gateway converts to base units

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--chain-id\fP=0
	EVM chain ID as listed in GET /blockchains (e.g. 5042002)

.PP
\fB-C\fP, \fB--charge\fP[=false]
	Create with mode=charge (immediate transfer, no escrow); default is authorize (escrow then capture)

.PP
\fB-d\fP, \fB--description\fP=""
	Optional reconciliation note (e.g. order id / invoice); prompted when omitted on a terminal

.PP
\fB-F\fP, \fB--from\fP=""
	Payer wallet address (from) (0x-prefixed, funds are pulled from here)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for create

.PP
\fB-f\fP, \fB--payment-file\fP=""
	Path to a JSON file with the full request body (overrides individual flags)

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--private-key\fP=""
	Payer's secp256k1 private key (0x-prefixed hex); creates the payment and signs locally

.PP
\fB-T\fP, \fB--to\fP=""
	Payee wallet address (to) (0x-prefixed, address from 'wallets')

.PP
\fB-t\fP, \fB--token\fP=""
	Token symbol as listed in GET /tokens (e.g. USDC)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payments create \\
    -F 0xBuyer… -T 0xMerchant… -t USDC -a 10.50 -c 5042002 \\
    -p 0xPayerKey…
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payments(1)\fP
